        <mxCell id="Z3S1CdWAG_eUmhvCRU8l-2" value="" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="46" y="930" width="718" height="479" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="dnchP8ELM1GfEOx9kYPy-1" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;In complex systems, Agents often need to interact with a variety of external resources, such as databases, APIs, and other services. Directly integrating each resource with the Agent can lead to tightly coupled code, making the system difficult to maintain and scale. MCP addresses this issue by providing a standardized protocol for communication. It defines a set of rules and conventions that Agents and external resources must adhere to, enabling seamless interaction and promoting modularity.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Key Concepts:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Agent: An entity that initiates communication with external resources through MCP. The Agent is responsible for formulating requests and processing responses.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;External Resource: A service or data source that provides functionality or information to the Agent. External resources expose their capabilities through the MCP interface.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;MCP Layer: The intermediary layer that facilitates communication between the Agent and the External Resource. It handles message routing, translation, and error handling.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Message: The unit of communication between the Agent and the External Resource. Messages are typically structured data, such as JSON or XML, that contain the request or response information.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Protocol: The set of rules and conventions that govern the format and exchange of messages between the Agent and the External Resource.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="10" y="440" width="724.5" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="dnchP8ELM1GfEOx9kYPy-3" value="Agent" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
